IMPORT prelude

-- National Research Fund Act 2006 (Singapore) -- what counts as "research and development activities" (s 3), who the Fund may
-- pay (s 5(2)), the Board's authorisation of every payment (s 7(2)), the secrecy offence for those administering the Fund (s 14),
-- forged documents and false statements in grant applications (s 15), liability of officers and partners (s 16), the Board and
-- Council members' duty to disclose an interest (s 17), and the Board's term and reporting deadlines (ss 9(2), 9(3)(f), (g), 12(2)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/NRFA2006.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021" and comes into operation on 31 December 2021. Its Legislative History lists only
-- Act 17 of 2006 (commenced 22 August 2006) and the 2007 Revised Edition (Chapter 201A); no amending Act is annotated.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0193 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. For a person or business the Act matters at one point: applying for, or receiving, money from the Fund.
-- SCOPED to that. Not encoded: what is paid into the Fund (s 4), its objects (s 5(1)), expenses and withdrawals beyond s 7(2)
-- (ss 6, 7(1)), the Fund's investments (s 5(3)), the Board's other functions (s 9(3)), the Council (s 10), accounts and audit
-- (ss 11, 12 other than the financial year, 13), the application of s 16 to foreign bodies (s 16(6)) and regulations (s 18).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Research Fund Act 2006 -- grants and offences`

§§ `3 -- research and development activities`

-- s 3(1)(a): "systematic, investigative or experimental activities that involve innovation and are carried on either wholly or partly
-- within Singapore" for the purpose of (i) "increasing or acquiring new knowledge" or (ii) "creating new or improved materials,
-- products, devices, processes or services";
-- (b): "other activities that are carried on either wholly or partly within Singapore for a purpose related to the carrying out of
-- activities of the kind mentioned in paragraph (a) or incidental or conducive to" it, "including" (i) information services such as
-- data collection, (ii) building expenditure, (iii) training and management of manpower, (iv) feasibility studies, (v) "patenting,
-- licensing and other activities".
-- s 3(2): the listed activities "must not be taken to be systematic, investigative or experimental activities": (a) market research,
-- (b) testing and standardisation, (c) prospecting for minerals, (d) cosmetic or stylistic changes, (e) pre-production such as
-- tooling-up and trial runs, (f) routine collection of information, (g) preparation for teaching, (h) routine software development,
-- (i) legal and administrative aspects of patenting "unless mentioned in subsection (1)(b)(v)", (j) statutory compliance,
-- (k) reverse engineering of a commercial product.
--
-- READING. s 3(2) takes its activities out of paragraph (a) only: it says they are not "systematic, investigative or experimental".
-- Nothing in the text takes them out of paragraph (b). So, read literally, market research or testing carried on for a purpose
-- related to a paragraph (a) project is still a research and development activity. This is an inference from the wording; the
-- cross-reference in (2)(i) to (1)(b)(v) suggests the drafters saw the overlap.
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `basic research for new knowledge`
    `experimental development of a new product`
    `data collection supporting research`
    `building a laboratory`
    `training research staff`
    `a feasibility study on research direction`
    `patenting research results`
    `market research`
    `testing and standardisation`
    `prospecting for minerals`
    `cosmetic changes to a product`
    `trial production runs`
    `preparation for teaching`
    `routine software development`
    `regulatory compliance work`
    `reverse engineering a commercial product`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is excluded from paragraph (a) by s 3(2)` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `market research` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `testing and standardisation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `prospecting for minerals` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `cosmetic changes to a product` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `trial production runs` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `preparation for teaching` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `routine software development` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `regulatory compliance work` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reverse engineering a commercial product` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Only the two research kinds are systematic, investigative or experimental by nature; the paragraph (b) kinds support them.
GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is systematic, investigative or experimental` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `basic research for new knowledge` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `experimental development of a new product` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity,
      `it involves innovation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it is carried on at least partly in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it is for a purpose related to a paragraph (a) activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a research and development activity` IF
        `it is carried on at least partly in Singapore`
    AND (    (    `is systematic, investigative or experimental` `the activity`
              AND (NOT `is excluded from paragraph (a) by s 3(2)` `the activity`)
              AND `it involves innovation`)
         OR  `it is for a purpose related to a paragraph (a) activity`)

§§ `5(2) and 7(2) -- who the Fund may pay`

-- s 5(2): moneys "may be withdrawn and applied for all or any of the following purposes only": (a) financial assistance "(including
-- loans and scholarships) to any public authority, enterprise, educational institution or other person (whether in Singapore or
-- elsewhere) undertaking or facilitating research and development activities"; (b) promoting or assisting an enterprise "engaged in
-- the exploitation of research and development activities" where the enterprise, "in the opinion of the Board" (i) "is profitable
-- and efficient or capable of becoming profitable and efficient; and" (ii) "has reasonable prospects for profitability, development,
-- expansion, growth or providing viable employment"; (c) remuneration of advisers "(other than public officers)".
-- s 7(2): "A payment must not be made out of the Fund unless the payment is authorised by the Board."
--
-- The recipient may be anywhere; the activity it undertakes must be carried on at least partly in Singapore (s 3).
GIVEN `undertakes or facilitates research and development` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the recipient is outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Board authorised the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Fund may give the person financial assistance` IF
        `undertakes or facilitates research and development`
    AND `the Board authorised the payment`

GIVEN `exploits research and development` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Board thinks it profitable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Board thinks it efficient` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Board thinks it capable of becoming profitable and efficient` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Board thinks it has reasonable prospects` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Board authorised the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Fund may assist the exploiting enterprise` IF
        `exploits research and development`
    AND (   (`the Board thinks it profitable` AND `the Board thinks it efficient`)
         OR `the Board thinks it capable of becoming profitable and efficient`)
    AND `the Board thinks it has reasonable prospects`
    AND `the Board authorised the payment`

GIVEN `advises the Board or Council` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Fund may remunerate the adviser` IF
    `advises the Board or Council` AND (NOT `is a public officer`)

§§ `14 -- secrecy of protected information`

-- s 14(4): "protected information" is information whose disclosure "would or could reasonably be expected to disclose a trade secret
-- or to adversely affect a person in relation to the lawful business affairs of that person".
-- s 14(1): a person "exercising any function under this Act" who obtains protected information about another "must not disclose"
-- it unless (a) with "the written consent" of the person it relates to, (b) for administering or enforcing the Act, or (c) in
-- compliance with a court, tribunal or other lawful authority.
-- s 14(3): disclosing includes "permitting any other person to have any access" to a record held "by virtue of the person being or
-- having been a member of the Board or Council".
GIVEN `it would reveal a trade secret` IS A BOOLEAN, `it would harm lawful business affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is protected information` IF
    `it would reveal a trade secret` OR `it would harm lawful business affairs`

GIVEN `told someone` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `let someone see the record` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `held the record as a Board or Council member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counts as disclosing` IF
    `told someone` OR (`let someone see the record` AND `held the record as a Board or Council member`)

GIVEN `exercises a function under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the information is protected` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `disclosed it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had written consent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `for administering the Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `required by a court or lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wrongful disclosure is an offence` IF
        `exercises a function under the Act`
    AND `the information is protected`
    AND `disclosed it`
    AND (NOT `had written consent`)
    AND (NOT `for administering the Act`)
    AND (NOT `required by a court or lawful authority`)

§§ `15 -- forgery and false statements`

-- s 15: an offence if a person (a) "forges or counterfeits any document or certificate required by the Board", or (b) in an
-- application to the Board "for its permission, consent or approval, or for any grant or financial assistance", makes or provides
-- a statement "which is false, and which the person either knows or believes to be false or does not believe to be true".
-- An honest mistake is not caught: the person must know or believe it false, or not believe it true.
GIVEN `forged a document required by the Board` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `made a statement in an application to the Board` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the statement is false` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or believed it false` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `did not believe it true` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a forgery or false statement offence` IF
        `forged a document required by the Board`
    OR  (    `made a statement in an application to the Board`
         AND `the statement is false`
         AND (`knew or believed it false` OR `did not believe it true`))

§§ `14(2) and 15 -- penalties`

-- s 14(2): "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both".
-- s 15: "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `wrongful disclosure`
    `forgery or false statement`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`maximum fine in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `wrongful disclosure` THEN 5000
    WHEN `forgery or false statement` THEN 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `wrongful disclosure` THEN 24
    WHEN `forgery or false statement` THEN 6

§§ `16 -- officers, partners and members of associations`

-- s 16(1): where an offence by a body corporate is proved "(a) to have been committed with the consent or connivance of an officer;
-- or (b) to be attributable to any neglect on the officer's part", the officer "as well as the body corporate" is guilty. (3) the
-- same for a partner of a partnership; (4) for an officer or governing-body member of an unincorporated association. (5) "body
-- corporate" includes a limited liability partnership; "officer" includes "any person purporting to act in any such capacity".
DECLARE Entity IS ONE OF
    `a company`
    `a limited liability partnership`
    `a partnership`
    `an unincorporated association`

GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity,
      `the entity committed an offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `holds or purports to hold the relevant position` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the offence is attributable to the individual's neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is also guilty` IF
        `the entity committed an offence under the Act`
    AND `holds or purports to hold the relevant position`
    AND (`consented or connived` OR `the offence is attributable to the individual's neglect`)

§§ `17 -- disclosure of interests`

-- s 17(1): a member of the Board or Council with "a direct or indirect pecuniary interest" in a matter before it, "being an interest
-- that could conflict with the proper performance of that member's functions", must disclose its nature "at a meeting" "as soon as
-- practicable"; (2) it must be recorded in the minutes. The Act creates no offence for failing to disclose.
GIVEN `is a Board or Council member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has a direct or indirect pecuniary interest in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the interest could conflict with the member's functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member must disclose the interest` IF
        `is a Board or Council member`
    AND `has a direct or indirect pecuniary interest in the matter`
    AND `the interest could conflict with the member's functions`

§§ `9(2), 9(3)(f), (g) and 12(2) -- term and deadlines`

-- s 9(2): each Board member "holds office for such period (not exceeding 3 years) as the Minister may in any case determine".
-- s 9(3)(f): the budget for the next year is due "not later than 30 days before the end of each financial year"; (g) the annual
-- report "not later than 30 days after the end of each financial year". s 12(2): the financial year is "12 months ending on
-- 31 March".
GIVEN `term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board appointment term is lawful` IF
    `term in years` > 0 AND `term in years` <= 3

GIVEN `days before 31 March` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the budget is submitted in time` IF
    `days before 31 March` >= 30

GIVEN `days after 31 March` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the annual report is submitted in time` IF
    `days after 31 March` <= 30
